Weekly Grocery Shopping Organization Guide
=========================================

Purpose: Help organize weekly grocery shopping efficiently and consistently.

Key Principles:
1. Plan ahead - Review past purchases and adjust based on habits
2. Group by store sections (produce, dairy, pantry, etc.)
3. Use a checklist for essential items
4. Set budget limits per category
5. Schedule shopping days/times that work best for you
6. Keep receipts for tracking spending
7. Update inventory regularly to avoid overbuying

Weekly Structure:
- Monday: Plan meals for the week, update pantry inventory
- Tuesday: Create weekly grocery list (based on meals + replenishment needs)
- Wednesday: Shop at main grocery store or split shopping days
- Thursday/Friday: Organize purchases by category, check off items as you shop
- Weekend: Use leftovers, review what's left in fridge/pantry for next week

Categories & Typical Items:
1. Produce (fresh fruits and vegetables)
   - Fruits: Apples, bananas, berries, oranges
   - Vegetables: Leafy greens, carrots, onions, tomatoes, seasonal options
   
2. Dairy & Alternatives
   - Milk, yogurt, cheese, eggs, plant-based milk/alternatives
   
3. Pantry Staples
   - Grains (rice, pasta, oats), canned goods, snacks, spices, oils
   
4. Meat & Seafood
   - Protein sources based on dietary needs and budget
   
5. Specialty Items
   - Organic options, ethnic ingredients, special dietary needs

Shopping Checklist Template:
[ ] Produce
  [ ] Fruit #1 (e.g., apples)
  [ ] Vegetable #1 (e.g., carrots)
  ...
[ ] Dairy & Alternatives
  [ ] Milk/dairy item
  [ ] Yogurt/cheese
...
[ ] Pantry Staples
  [ ] Rice or pasta
  [ ] Canned goods
...
[ ] Meat & Seafood
  [ ] Protein choice

Budget Tracker (per category):
- Produce: $X.XX
- Dairy: $X.XX  
- Pantry: $X.XX
- Meat/Seafood: $X.XX
- Total Budget: $XXX.XX

Inventory Log (update weekly):
Date | Item                | Quantity Remaining | Notes
-----|--------------------|-------------------|------
     |                    |                   |     